schema: test/v2
level: working-unit
epic: E-REDESIGN
wu: E-REDESIGN.W2
tests:
  unit:
    added:
      - "ui/src/components/Field.test.tsx — 8 tests. Every keystroke reports undebounced with no internal value state (B1); the value renders from the caller and a change without a re-render does not stick; no validity is ever expressed for any input including a malformed status, and inputMode passes through without restricting (B2); the accessible name is a prop and the placeholder is NOT queryable as a name (B3); width comes only from the caller's class (B4); hover and focus both land on the border with no ring (driver ④); disabled dims and leaves the tab order. The load-bearing one is F2: Field and Select are rendered together and asserted to share min-h-control, rounded-button, border-hairline, px-control-x, py-control-y and text-control, with px-3 and py-chrome-y asserted ABSENT — so a build that copies the legacy class string fails rather than passes."
      - "ui/src/components/StatusDot.test.tsx — 7 tests. The three fills map from status alone (B1); every state's accessible name carries its phrase from COPY.dotTitle, so the button is never nameless (B2/S4 — the shipped defect); the disc is aria-hidden and carries data-status, so the verdict announces once; the hit target is the 24px button and the 10px disc is not a BUTTON (S3 — the shipped defect); clickable and not disabled in all three states including connected (B3); hover is a wash on the button and never on the fill; no animation on checking."
      - "ui/src/components/Disclosure.test.tsx — 8 tests. It is a native <details> whose summary carries no hand-written role, tabIndex or aria-expanded (D1/B2); defaultOpen seeds and a re-render does not yank a user-closed panel open (B1); the UA marker is suppressed both ways and the app's glyph is present (D3); one glyph rotates rather than two swapping, and the rotate-90 rule is on the element (D2); the summary row is the full-width target at the hit floor (driver ⑦); the slot's class list is EXACTLY mt-chrome-y — no border, padding, indent or cap (anatomy ③); it never inspects what it hides."
  integration:
    extended:
      - "ui/src/components/collection.test.tsx — the collection's own contract, which IS this WU's bounded contract: the barrel matches the TSDoc roster exactly, every roster name has a mounting specimen, every @madeof edge composes, and every @avoid redirect resolves to an export. Three specimens added. The @madeof assertion for CopyButton/IconButton was widened to include StatusDot — four components, one <button> each, all carrying Button's focus ring and disabled treatment, none nesting a second button. The redirect assertion is DERIVED from the roster, so KeyValueRow→Field, StatusPill→StatusDot and Section→Disclosure entered it by the components existing; that is the epic's phantom-redirect closure becoming a check rather than prose (528 → 529 tests, the +1 being Section's newly-live redirect)."
  e2e:
    waived: "No user-visible surface moves. The three components have no call site yet — git diff epic/redesign..HEAD -- 'ui/src/*.tsx' is empty — so every screen renders exactly what it rendered before and there is nothing for a UC spec to observe that it does not already assert. This is the epic plan's stated shape: W2 unblocks the four screen runs, and the e2e that proves these components on screen is UC-4's (W4) and UC-ONBOARD's (W10)."
verified:
  - "cd ui && pnpm test — 529 passed, 43 files, 0 failed."
  - "cd ui && pnpm exec eslint src — clean, including the two new tailwind scale members."
  - "cd ui && pnpm build — tsc -b + vite green."
  - "node scripts/design-registry.mjs — 27 entries; the oracle throws on any @tier block missing a tag, so a short roster cannot pass silently."
  - "Emitted CSS, not just the config: dist/assets/index-*.css carries `rotate-90{--tw-rotate: 90deg;…}`, the `[open]>summary>[data-twist]` variant, and `transition-property:transform`. Checked in the OUTPUT because DEC-17's failure mode is a class that resolves to nothing without erroring — the config declaring a scale is not evidence the utility emits."
  - "DEC-16 step ② — each of the six TSDoc tags parsed out of both the design file's compile block (at HEAD~1, before deletion) and the shipped .tsx, then compared: all three byte-identical. This is the check that licenses step ③."
  - "cargo xtask verify-doc — green on the W2 plan (wu-plan), the W2 result (wu-result), DEC-30 and the decisions index. components·unretired confirmed RED on all three design files after the build commit and gone after the retirement commit — the check firing is itself evidence the retirement was owed here and not deferrable."
  - "cargo test + cargo xtask gate0 — green. No Rust changed; run because the gate re-walks it."
  - "cargo xtask ui specimens --check — every remaining design artifact still renders over file:// with a clean console."
  - "Real-browser measurement, not jsdom: a Vite page built from the actual components, read in headless Chrome. Field h=25.25 pad=3px/9px r=3px b=1px rgb(63,58,54) font=11.5px, IDENTICAL to Select's trigger on all six (F2). StatusDot's button 24x24 around a 10x10 disc (S3). aria-label 'Not capturing yet — click to set up' (S4). The twist: matrix(1,0,0,1,0,0) closed → matrix(0,1,-1,0,0,0) open, exactly 90° (D2). Summary rgb(174,166,156) → rgb(247,245,240) on open. Scaffolding removed after the reading; the screenshot is in the result report."
note: "One test was rewritten after it failed, and the reason is on the record rather than in a silent fixup. Field's B1 test first read onChange.mock.calls[i][0].target.value and saw three empty strings — a test artifact, not a component defect: the input is controlled at value=\"\", so React resets target.value before the stored event reference is read. Rewritten to capture the value inside the handler at call time and to re-render with each new value, the way a real controlled parent does. No unit test covers deviation D1 (test hooks on the disc rather than the button) as a CONTRACT — the tests query [data-status] where it actually is, and the anatomy line in the TSDoc still says what the design said, deliberately unedited so the divergence stays visible to W4 rather than being smoothed away."
